    "decision": "accept",
    "reason": "The complete139 chain152→154→156→157→159→176→177→179→180→182→183→194 explicitly depends on sound substitutions, not just alternative business ideas. Retain the English source slogan endings with Czech meaning glosses. Plume/Zoom/COOM share the English long-u and m ending; Spoon/Poon retain the source's long-u near-rhyme with n rather than pretend they are perfect Czech rhymes. Existing Czech transport title Letem světem remains identified in156 and unchanged in all nine other base-brand occurrences. Cuddling and vulva alternatives, ejaculation, stammer, mockery and rebuttal all remain. This is a foreign-language wordplay adaptation requiring independent evaluation, not a native-rhyme claim.",
    "proposal": "repair route accepted; actual new complete wording authored here",
